  "problem": "$8q+(6p+5q)\\cdot (-2)=${{field-1}}\n$q\\,-$\n{{field-2}}$p$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we distribute the $(-2)$ over each of the terms in parentheses.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8q+(6p+5q)\\cdot (-2) & = \\\\ 8q+6p\\cdot (-2)+5q\\cdot (-2) & = \\\\ 8q+(-12p)+(-10q) & = \\\\ 8q-12p-10q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8q-12p-10q & = \\\\ (8q-10q)-12p & = \\\\ -2\\,q-12\\,p & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
